  "id": "Compound::DB01023 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Felodipine, a calcium channel blocker, exhibits a complex interaction with cytochrome P450 enzymes, particularly Cyp2c8. The evidence suggests that Felodipine binds to Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, both of which are involved in oxidoreductive activities, and these enzymes are further implicated in Cyp2c8. This indicates a potential mechanism where Felodipine may modulate Cyp2c8 through interactions with its substrates, possibly affecting enzyme activity or expression. The observed scores in the paths highlight a consistent pattern of Felodipine binding to Cyp2c8 through different pathways, suggesting a plausible mechanism of action involving enzyme inhibition or modulation. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Felodipine may influence Cyp2c8 through a shared functional role in metabolic processes, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
